# Keep the build context small and credentials out of it. The Dockerfile's build
# stage does COPY . ., so secret-file patterns are depth-matched (**/) — a
# .gitignored local secret at any level stays out of the context and its cache.
node_modules
.next
.git
coverage
playwright-report
test-results
# Parallel-session worktrees: each is a whole extra checkout under the repo root,
# so without this every live worktree lands in the build context.
.claude/worktrees
**/.env*
# google-github-actions/auth writes its federated credential into the workspace
# as gha-creds-*.json, and the delivery workflow's `docker build .` has the
# workspace as its context. The multi-stage build means it never reaches the
# pushed image — only .next/standalone, .next/static and public are copied
# forward — but it would otherwise sit in the build stage's layer and its cache
# for the life of the job.
**/gha-creds-*.json
*.pem
*.log
